# fc_pnr_paper_core.tcl - Fusion Compiler P&R for the ON-DIE digital core.
#
# DERIVED FROM : fc_pnr_v4paper.tcl
#
# The derivation changes exactly SIX things, every one of them a path, a name, or
# a guard - never an algorithm or an option:
#
#   1. PRJ   -> /home/<user>/sar16_work/proj_paper_core   (self-contained)
#   2. NET   -> $PRJ/mapped_ss/sar_digi_paper_core_netlist.v
#               the DESIGN COMPILER SLOW ARM, matched to the NDM's corner.
#   3. SDC   -> $PRJ/constraints/sar_digi_paper_core_pnr.sdc
#   4. TOP   -> sar_digi_paper_core
#   5. library name -> sar16_pnr_paper_core.  Unique per arm on purpose: the v3.0
#               accident was three runs all using a library called `sar16_pnr`
#               and exporting from the same working directory, so two of the
#               three delivered GDS files were a later run's output.
#   6. the pre-flight asserts the netlist really lives in proj_paper_core.
#
# NDM, TDB, TLU+, layer map and UTIL are REUSED unchanged.  They are library and
# technology facts, identical for both blocks, and reusing them is what makes the
# core's physical numbers comparable to the integrated top's.
#
# NO POWER PLAN: no UPF, no PG pins; VDD/VSS come from the enclosing analog top.
# Signal routing and timing are unaffected, but the GDS is NOT tapeout-ready in
# the power sense.
# =============================================================================
